WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.956
In squiggly careers, we need to 
change&nbsp;our perspective on progression.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.172
The problem with career ladders is&nbsp;
that they only go in one direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:10.555
and you can only take one step at a time.

00:00:11.151 --> 00:00:13.923
If progression purely means promotion,

00:00:13.923 --> 00:00:17.146
we miss out on so many of the 
opportunities that&nbsp;are all around us.

00:00:17.832 --> 00:00:21.228
We need to stop asking 
only, "What job comes next?"

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:25.483
and start asking, "What&nbsp;career
possibilities am I curious about?".

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.331
Exploring our career possibilities 
increases&nbsp;our resilience.

00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:32.425
It gives us more options,

00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:34.754
and you create more connections.

00:00:34.754 --> 00:00:38.917
In squiggly&nbsp;careers, there is 
room for everybody to succeed.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:41.283
And no two squiggles are the same.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.678
The ladder&nbsp;has been holding 
us back for far too long.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.000
But it's not easy to change something 
that's&nbsp;been around for over 100 years.

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:53.795
What we need now is more 
than a radical rethink.

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.100
We need&nbsp;a radical redo,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.521
and change comes from action.

